WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:06.900
So we get a lot of questions from
people who work in toxic leadership environments

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.803
and they ask,
what are they to do?

00:00:08.803 --> 00:00:11.300
How do they 
be the leader they wish they had?

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:15.260
Well, being the leader you wish you had
means you commit yourself

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.639
to the care and success of
those around you.

00:00:17.639 --> 00:00:19.500
Remember, leadership has nothing to do with rank.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:23.210
I know many people who sit
at the highest levels of organizations

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:27.409
who are not leaders.
They have authority, which is why we do as they tell us

00:00:27.409 --> 00:00:30.891
but we would not follow them. 
Leadership can happen at any rank.

00:00:30.891 --> 00:00:31.909
The choice you have to make is

00:00:31.909 --> 00:00:35.629
do you want to be the leader?
Now leadership comes with risks.

00:00:35.629 --> 00:00:37.802
If you speak truth to power,
you could get in trouble.

00:00:37.802 --> 00:00:39.800
If you're the one who stands in between

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:43.200
the powers that be
and the people that you work with,

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.500
if you're gonna commit yourself

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:48.050
to work late sometimes
to help people and make those sacrifices,

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:50.451
you're gonna have to take those risks.

00:00:50.451 --> 00:00:52.600
That's why not everyone wants to be a leader

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:55.900
because it does come with real
sacrifice and real risk.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:56.900
But if you want to be that person,

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:59.003
if you want to be the leader
you wish you had,

00:00:59.003 --> 00:01:00.500
you look to your left,
you look to your right

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:01.900
and you say,
how can I help them succeed?

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:04.800
Number one: 
if you see somebody on your team struggling

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.320
ask them if they're okay.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:10.460
Ask them if you can help.
If you know that somebody doesn't know

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:13.300
how to do something, sit down and show them.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:16.960
Ask them if you want them to 
double check your work.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:20.540
Remember, a big way in which
we build trust is not actually by

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:23.136
offering for help but also
asking for help.

00:01:23.136 --> 00:01:25.189
So one of the things you can do

00:01:25.189 --> 00:01:28.026
by being a leader is also asking for those
around you to help.

00:01:28.026 --> 00:01:28.850
Let them feel like they're empowered

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:32.420
to help those around them
and in the course of time you will

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:35.500
build a level of trust on your team
that they will see you as the person

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:36.900
who has their back.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:41.060
And you get used to it.
It's a practice like many other

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:43.425
like any other skills.
You want to ride a bicycle,

00:01:43.425 --> 00:01:44.900
you have to practice,
you get good at it.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:47.434
Leadership is the same.

00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:50.180
Get in the habit of
considering the lives of others.

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:53.270
If someone's running for the elevator,
the doors are closing,

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:56.420
you're running late for a meeting. 
Instead of just letting the doors close,

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:59.300
hold the door open for somebody. 
If you're the last person to pour yourself

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:02.220
a cup of coffee at the office, 
instead of putting the empty pot back

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:03.300
make another pot of coffee.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:06.900
It's little, little things
where you consider those around you,

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:09.350
the lives of others,
sometimes ahead of yourself

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:14.000
and be willing to sacrifice time and energy
to help those around you.

